1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,106
This is a screen recording of the lead enrichment project in a local browser workspace.

2
00:00:05,226 --> 00:00:10,682
The source viewer reads actual project files, and the terminal runs the Python program.

3
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,079
Narration is synthetic.

4
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:18,839
The project separates crawling, cleaning, extraction, and orchestration.

5
00:00:18,959 --> 00:00:24,647
The input is a JSON array containing the three assignment targets: Postman, Supabase, and Vapi.

6
00:00:24,767 --> 00:00:28,100
The README explains environment setup and local execution.

7
00:00:29,369 --> 00:00:33,085
I am starting the command with NVIDIA and the free tier only guard enabled.

8
00:00:33,205 --> 00:00:36,235
This terminal displays the actual process output.

9
00:00:36,355 --> 00:00:41,742
The three companies are processed concurrently, using headless Chromium to render their public websites.

10
00:00:45,369 --> 00:00:47,726
The crawler discovers relevant company links.

11
00:00:47,846 --> 00:00:53,373
The cleaner removes scripts, styles, SVG elements, and navigation boilerplate.

12
00:00:53,493 --> 00:00:58,125
It preserves readable text, public emails, and profile associations.

13
00:00:58,245 --> 00:01:03,818
The bounded context sent to the language model contains clean evidence, not raw HTML trees.

14
00:01:05,088 --> 00:01:11,903
Pydantic defines the required overview, target audience, contacts, leadership details, and confidence score.

15
00:01:12,023 --> 00:01:14,391
The overview must contain two sentences.

16
00:01:14,511 --> 00:01:16,845
Confidence is bounded from zero to one.

17
00:01:16,965 --> 00:01:21,969
The extractor checks the schema and verifies that reported entities have supporting evidence.

18
00:01:23,239 --> 00:01:25,503
Each company has its own failure boundary.

19
00:01:25,623 --> 00:01:32,519
Missing pages, timeouts, bot blockers, and provider errors are recorded, with bounded retries where appropriate.

20
00:01:32,639 --> 00:01:34,346
The other companies can continue.

21
00:01:34,466 --> 00:01:38,193
I will remove the remaining waiting time and return to the finished output.

22
00:01:39,462 --> 00:01:40,879
The pipeline has finished.

23
00:01:40,999 --> 00:01:44,377
This is the Postman record generated by the command just shown.

24
00:01:44,497 --> 00:01:50,569
It includes the company overview, audience, public emails, leadership details, and confidence.

25
00:01:50,689 --> 00:01:54,915
Source pages, crawl errors, and token usage are included for review.

26
00:01:57,462 --> 00:02:00,307
The combined JSON includes all three companies.

27
00:02:00,427 --> 00:02:02,540
Here are the Supabase and Vapi records.

28
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:06,213
Information that the collected pages do not support is left empty.

29
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:10,733
Confidence reflects evidence completeness, rather than guaranteeing every fact.

30
00:02:12,003 --> 00:02:14,952
I am now running the saved output verifier in the terminal.

31
00:02:15,072 --> 00:02:20,958
It checks the schema, two sentence summaries, entity evidence, page limits, and token totals.

32
00:02:21,078 --> 00:02:22,657
All three records pass.

33
00:02:22,777 --> 00:02:25,946
This validation does not make another language model call.

34
00:02:30,003 --> 00:02:34,113
The summary records actual token usage and estimated cost per domain.

35
00:02:34,233 --> 00:02:38,122
The zero dollar estimate uses the configured NVIDIA free tier rates.

36
00:02:38,242 --> 00:02:45,870
The repository includes modular code, dependencies, setup instructions, tests, sample output, and this screen recording.

37
00:02:45,990 --> 00:02:46,698
Thank you.
